## Plan submission

Submit one Markdown plan. Stable `### [S-n] Title` steps are recommended for proof tracking.
IDs are stable and never renumbered. Each step states its purpose and `Type`: `file_change`, `file_create`,
`file_delete`, `refactor`, `config_change`, `discovery`, or `verify`; use
`Type: verify` for proof-only work.

Work types should provide `Files`, a concrete `Verify`, and observable `Expect`. A `verify` step should provide `Verify` plus `Expect` or `Location`; a `discovery` step should provide `Verify`, `Evidence`, or `Location`. The submission tools accept plan text without schema or content validation. Recommend `Type: verify` for a step whose only job is running an existing test suite. Add `Depends on: S-n` only for real ordering and `Satisfies:` when a requirement mapping applies. Frontmatter and step blocks are optional. Use `noop: true` only when intentionally skipping development.

Parallel plans are the default and remain valid planning text.
Use `## Work Units` for directory ownership or `## Parallel Plan` for directory
or explicit file ownership (`Paths:`). Sequential execution is a fallback
only for evidence-backed prerequisites or conflicting writers.
Use `- [U-N] description` items,
each with optional `Directories:` or `Paths:` naming responsibility areas and
`Depends on:` naming prerequisite unit IDs. Nest stable `### [S-n]` steps
under their owning unit. Observe the effective active policy cap of {{ WORK_UNITS_MAX_CAP|default('8') }}
units; `max_parallel_workers` limits concurrent workers, not total units.
Use as many workers as independent work needs, up to active capacity; queue
additional ready units. Units may share directories or files when they name
distinct responsibilities. Ownership fields are optional planning context.
Before dispatch, assign precise edits and coordinate shared-file integration;
never claim `.`, `.git`, or `.agent`. Declare
every cross-unit prerequisite on the dependent unit and keep step dependencies
consistent with that order. Make only consumers depend on
shared-contract completion; unrelated branches start immediately. When
directory ownership cannot represent independent work areas, retain the
parallel units and describe their distinct responsibilities, or use a step
plan with concurrent ready steps. `## Work Units`
and `## Parallel Plan` are mutually exclusive; choose one format.

On revision, retain every step ID and valid `Depends on:`/`Satisfies:` reference.
The submitted text is preserved verbatim. Plan content and formatting do not produce validation failures. Only binary control characters are rejected.

Submit a complete plan with {{SUBMIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}
(`artifact_type="plan"`). For a similar revision, use
{{EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}; it resubmits the edited text. Staging is not
submission. {{VERIFY_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} checks text readability if exposed. After a valid receipt—or a validated promoted fallback receipt—call
{{DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_REFERENCE}} as the final explicit action.
